# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: One by one, the eight Old Fears of the valley fell before your blades, their long nightmares dissolving into the wet moorland grass.
Narrator: When Kehlenn held out her hand with one last whispered bargain, you turned away and left her offer in the dust.
Narrator: A deep tremor runs through the hills of Druskenvald as the fallen bulk of the moon begins to lift from the crushed horizon.
Narrator: Slowly, quietly, the pale sphere climbs back into the high vault of heaven, shedding the dust and briars of the earth.
Narrator: As it rises, the leering crone's face softens and fades from the silver stone, leaving only a clean, quiet lantern in the dark.
the_vagrant [smile]: Well now, I have ridden these rails a long while, and I never thought to see that old face wiped clean.
Narrator: A gentle wind sweeps across the Founder's Round, carrying the scent of rain and fresh clover to a world made strange and new.
-> END
